WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.919
STUDENT COUNCIL OFFICE

00:03.002 --> 00:04.504
As for my hobbies,

00:04.587 --> 00:06.089
I'm into all kinds of otaku interests.

00:06.589 --> 00:08.216
I know most of the anime and manga

00:08.299 --> 00:10.135
that are popular these days.

00:10.218 --> 00:11.094
That's all.

00:11.594 --> 00:12.679
Thank you.

00:13.263 --> 00:16.307
With this, Kuze is an official member
of the student council.

00:16.391 --> 00:19.811
Can you please work with Mariya today?

00:19.894 --> 00:20.812
Sure.

00:20.895 --> 00:22.188
I'm sorry.

00:22.272 --> 00:23.189
Well,

00:23.273 --> 00:26.317
you were the vice president
in junior high.

00:26.401 --> 00:28.111
You'll get the hang of it soon.

00:28.194 --> 00:29.738
But for now, follow the members

00:29.821 --> 00:31.698
and learn about the job.

00:31.781 --> 00:34.075
Is it because you're short-staffed?

00:34.159 --> 00:36.995
Yes, to be honest,
we're lacking in manpower.

00:37.078 --> 00:38.705
Sorry to interrupt your conversation.

00:39.497 --> 00:41.916
About the exhibition,

00:42.000 --> 00:45.128
I'd like to discuss it with the art club.

00:45.211 --> 00:46.504
I'm counting on you.

00:46.588 --> 00:47.464
Okay.

00:48.047 --> 00:49.424
Also,

00:50.008 --> 00:52.469
since we'll be discussing the budget,

00:52.552 --> 00:56.139
I'd like the treasurer Alisa
to come with me.

00:56.222 --> 00:57.057
What?

00:59.559 --> 01:00.977
All right.

01:01.061 --> 01:03.438
President, I'll be back in a bit.

01:03.521 --> 01:05.190
Okay, thank you.

01:08.943 --> 01:11.905
<i>Judging from this situation,
she must have some other purpose.</i>

02:48.877 --> 02:49.794
<i>I should be</i>

02:49.878 --> 02:52.422
<i>the one to bring this up first.</i>

02:53.923 --> 02:54.924
Suou.

02:55.925 --> 02:58.219
Do you have a minute?

02:58.303 --> 02:59.304
Sure.

02:59.971 --> 03:04.183
Why don't we use that empty classroom?

03:07.687 --> 03:08.897
I've decided

03:08.980 --> 03:12.650
to run for student council
president with Kuze.

03:12.734 --> 03:14.986
Yes, I know.

03:15.069 --> 03:18.406
Masachika told me about it yesterday.

03:18.990 --> 03:19.908
I see.

03:21.200 --> 03:23.620
Well, is this what you wanted
to talk about?

03:23.703 --> 03:27.123
Yes. I didn't do anything wrong.

03:27.206 --> 03:29.000
So I don't intend to apologize.

03:29.083 --> 03:32.795
I just wanted to tell you in person.

03:34.297 --> 03:35.715
I see.

03:36.216 --> 03:37.342
Indeed,

03:37.425 --> 03:40.011
you don't have to apologize to me.

03:40.678 --> 03:44.515
Because it was Masachika's choice.

03:45.099 --> 03:48.269
I have no complaints about that.

03:48.853 --> 03:51.689
Nor do I want to vent
my frustrations to you.

03:53.441 --> 03:54.692
It's a shame

03:54.776 --> 03:57.904
that he didn't choose me, though.

03:59.739 --> 04:01.115
Suou.

04:01.199 --> 04:02.784
Is Kuze your...

04:03.743 --> 04:05.912
No, it's nothing.

04:05.995 --> 04:07.622
I love him.

04:08.623 --> 04:10.500
More than anyone in the world.

04:11.000 --> 04:13.211
More than anyone?

04:13.294 --> 04:14.295
Yes.

04:14.879 --> 04:16.297
Compared to my love for my mother

04:16.381 --> 04:17.882
and father,

04:17.966 --> 04:20.593
my love for Masachika

04:20.677 --> 04:22.053
is much greater.

04:24.138 --> 04:25.765
What about you, Alisa?

04:25.848 --> 04:26.766
What?

04:26.849 --> 04:30.603
How do you feel about Masachika?

04:30.687 --> 04:33.314
I...

04:34.691 --> 04:37.527
Kuze is my friend.

04:37.610 --> 04:39.946
A very important friend.

04:40.029 --> 04:41.322
Do you like him?

04:41.406 --> 04:42.323
What?

04:42.407 --> 04:43.700
So what is it?

04:44.534 --> 04:45.827
Do you like him?

04:45.910 --> 04:48.329
"Like"?

04:48.413 --> 04:49.789
Well, this feeling...

04:50.790 --> 04:53.584
I've made it clear that I love him.

04:53.668 --> 04:54.961
Alisa,

04:55.044 --> 04:56.838
you should be clear too.

05:03.011 --> 05:05.179
Although I don't know

05:05.263 --> 05:06.931
if I like him or not,

05:07.765 --> 05:09.058
I will never

05:10.685 --> 05:12.228
let you have Kuze!

05:15.982 --> 05:17.191
I see.

05:18.359 --> 05:20.320
Anyway,

05:20.403 --> 05:23.114
hearing you say that today
is enough for me.

05:25.158 --> 05:27.702
Well then, let's go to the art club.

05:27.785 --> 05:29.162
Okay.

05:31.873 --> 05:33.166
Right.

05:34.167 --> 05:35.126
If you don't mind,

05:35.209 --> 05:37.670
can I call you Alya too?

05:37.754 --> 05:40.965
I always hear Masha
and Masachika call you that.

05:41.049 --> 05:43.634
I find this nickname very cute.

05:43.718 --> 05:46.220
That's fine.

05:46.304 --> 05:49.974
Please call me Yuki from now on too.

05:51.851 --> 05:53.895
Yuki.

05:53.978 --> 05:55.354
I'm so happy.

05:58.483 --> 05:59.567
I think...

05:59.650 --> 06:03.112
I just blurted out something outrageous.

06:04.572 --> 06:06.991
Masha, about this part...

06:08.493 --> 06:10.078
There's a mistake here.

06:10.161 --> 06:12.371
Is that so?

06:12.455 --> 06:14.332
I'll fix it then.

06:14.415 --> 06:16.000
Yes, please.

06:17.043 --> 06:18.961
<i>Is she for real?</i>

06:19.545 --> 06:21.714
<i>She's really good at her job.</i>

06:22.548 --> 06:25.343
<i>On the other hand...</i>

06:25.426 --> 06:29.263
This. I think I saw it somewhere.

06:30.098 --> 06:31.974
Wait, why did this happen?

06:33.309 --> 06:34.977
Chisaki.

06:35.061 --> 06:38.523
The library is going to change
its collection of books today.

06:38.606 --> 06:40.108
I heard they're short-staffed.

06:40.650 --> 06:42.110
Leave it to me!

06:46.072 --> 06:47.740
I'm sorry, Kuze.

06:47.824 --> 06:50.368
That's just how Chisaki is.

06:50.451 --> 06:51.410
It may not seem so,

06:51.494 --> 06:53.621
but she's the best at coordinating

06:53.704 --> 06:55.498
between committees and clubs.

06:55.581 --> 06:56.415
It's fine.

06:56.499 --> 06:59.001
This is putting the right person
in the right place.

07:01.420 --> 07:03.714
Let's take a break.

07:03.798 --> 07:05.174
I'll make some black tea.

07:05.258 --> 07:07.301
Let me help.

07:07.385 --> 07:09.095
It's okay.

07:10.471 --> 07:11.889
Just sit and wait.

07:12.390 --> 07:15.393
I love making tea.

07:17.061 --> 07:19.188
Kuze, do you like your tea with milk?

07:19.272 --> 07:20.314
Or sugar?

07:21.107 --> 07:22.608
There's jam too.

07:22.692 --> 07:23.901
Jam?

07:23.985 --> 07:25.820
Could that be Russian tea?

07:25.903 --> 07:28.197
Since I'm here, I'll add some jam.

07:28.281 --> 07:29.407
Okay.

07:29.907 --> 07:32.452
President, you're fine
with protein powder, right?

07:32.535 --> 07:34.120
How's that fine?

07:35.037 --> 07:38.291
I didn't know you made jokes like that.

07:39.584 --> 07:40.751
What?

07:40.835 --> 07:41.794
In Russia,

07:41.878 --> 07:44.964
isn't black tea a winter beverage?

07:46.090 --> 07:48.426
I think it's different for every family.

07:48.509 --> 07:49.927
At least in my family,

07:50.011 --> 07:52.180
we drink black tea in the summer too.

07:53.764 --> 07:54.724
Well,

07:54.807 --> 07:57.768
it's because my mom loves black tea.

07:58.269 --> 08:00.688
Your mom is Japanese, after all.

08:01.189 --> 08:02.231
Kuze,

08:02.315 --> 08:04.066
do you know a lot about Russia?

08:04.650 --> 08:05.902
Not really.

08:05.985 --> 08:10.114
I just watched a few Russian movies
with my grandpa.

08:11.199 --> 08:12.325
I see.

08:12.408 --> 08:15.578
<i>But that was just the starting point.</i>

08:15.661 --> 08:17.788
<i>I actually studied really hard</i>

08:17.872 --> 08:20.333
<i>just to talk to that girl.</i>

08:22.418 --> 08:24.462
Here you go, thank you for waiting.

08:25.421 --> 08:27.298
Thank you.

08:31.802 --> 08:32.803
It's delicious.

08:33.387 --> 08:35.139
Really? Thank you.

08:37.391 --> 08:39.810
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

08:40.853 --> 08:42.396
<i>it seemed that Mother</i>

08:42.480 --> 08:44.023
<i>liked black tea too.</i>

08:53.157 --> 08:56.619
So you don't add the jam
directly to the tea?

08:56.702 --> 08:58.621
It depends on the person.

08:58.704 --> 08:59.705
I see.

09:05.920 --> 09:06.796
So sweet.

09:08.130 --> 09:09.674
We're back.

09:10.508 --> 09:11.801
I'm back.

09:11.884 --> 09:13.678
Welcome back.

09:13.761 --> 09:15.221
Would you like some tea?

09:15.304 --> 09:17.014
I'd love some.

09:17.723 --> 09:18.683
Yes.

09:18.766 --> 09:19.809
Okay.

09:19.892 --> 09:21.769
Just a moment.

09:28.651 --> 09:29.485
What is it?

09:29.569 --> 09:31.445
Don't you think you're too close?

09:31.529 --> 09:32.738
In Russia,

09:32.822 --> 09:36.409
it's bad luck for a young woman
to sit in the corner.

09:36.492 --> 09:37.702
Is that so?

09:37.785 --> 09:38.703
Yes.

09:38.786 --> 09:40.955
<i>No, but this is way too close!</i>

09:46.294 --> 09:48.087
<i>What? Love triangle?</i>

09:48.170 --> 09:49.714
<i>Is this a love triangle?</i>

09:50.464 --> 09:51.716
Hey, Masha.

09:51.799 --> 09:53.426
Regarding what Alya just said,

09:53.509 --> 09:56.012
is there such a jinx in Russia?

09:56.095 --> 09:57.305
Yes.

09:57.388 --> 09:58.389
But to be exact,

09:58.472 --> 10:00.933
it is said that it could delay
a woman's prospects for marriage.

10:01.434 --> 10:05.730
Alya, have you met someone
you want to marry?

10:05.813 --> 10:07.315
Of course not.

10:07.398 --> 10:08.608
It's just a whim.

10:08.691 --> 10:11.235
Hey, really?

10:11.319 --> 10:12.737
You're so annoying.

10:14.071 --> 10:16.282
If it's "marriage", then it's too early.

10:16.824 --> 10:19.910
<i>Yes, you're only 15 years old.</i>

10:19.994 --> 10:22.038
<i>The way you put it bothers me though.</i>

10:22.538 --> 10:24.749
<i>Your sister is here!
How could you say that in Russian?</i>

10:25.583 --> 10:27.084
Here, Alya.

10:27.585 --> 10:29.086
Eat this first.

10:34.467 --> 10:35.384
What is it?

10:35.468 --> 10:36.594
No, it's nothing.

10:37.803 --> 10:40.473
Okay, that's all for today.

10:41.057 --> 10:43.809
We sophomores have something
to discuss with the teacher.

10:43.893 --> 10:46.020
The freshmen can go home now.

10:46.103 --> 10:47.480
Thank you, everyone.

10:47.563 --> 10:49.357
- Thank you for your hard work.
- Thank you for your hard work.

10:54.820 --> 10:58.240
<i>That brat Yuki
must have said something to Alya.</i>

10:58.324 --> 10:59.992
ROYAL FAST

11:00.701 --> 11:02.203
Alya.

11:02.286 --> 11:03.412
What's wrong?

11:03.496 --> 11:05.456
If you don't mind,
would you like to stop by?

11:05.539 --> 11:06.374
What?

11:07.458 --> 11:08.376
Why?

11:08.459 --> 11:11.921
Nothing much. I just thought that
since we're aiming for the presidency,

11:12.004 --> 11:14.215
we should discuss various issues first.

11:15.966 --> 11:17.468
Well, I'm okay with that.

11:17.551 --> 11:18.928
Let's go inside then.

11:20.388 --> 11:22.515
So it isn't a date?

11:23.474 --> 11:26.394
<i>Is that what you thought?</i>

11:26.477 --> 11:28.104
<i>Alya!</i>

11:33.025 --> 11:33.901
What?

11:33.984 --> 11:35.319
No, it's nothing.

11:35.986 --> 11:38.114
Because I'm a little tired.

11:38.197 --> 11:41.200
If I don't eat something sweet,
I can't think straight.

11:41.283 --> 11:42.410
I see.

11:43.619 --> 11:44.995
Well,

11:45.079 --> 11:46.831
did something happen with Yuki?

11:48.165 --> 11:49.333
No.

11:49.417 --> 11:50.793
<i>Yuki!</i>

11:50.876 --> 11:53.087
<i>What the heck did you do?!</i>

11:54.255 --> 11:55.297
Are you

11:55.381 --> 11:57.133
dating Yuki?

11:57.216 --> 11:58.426
Of course not.

11:59.677 --> 12:00.594
You're not?

12:00.678 --> 12:02.513
No. Definitely not.

12:02.596 --> 12:04.515
But Yuki said...

12:06.142 --> 12:08.436
This is a good chance to clear things up.

12:08.519 --> 12:11.188
She's not as ladylike as she looks.

12:11.689 --> 12:12.982
She's just teasing you.

12:13.065 --> 12:15.317
The more you panic, the happier she gets.

12:16.735 --> 12:17.570
All right.

12:17.653 --> 12:19.822
Let's talk about
the presidential election.

12:20.406 --> 12:21.574
Let me be blunt.

12:21.657 --> 12:24.201
At this rate,
you won't be able to beat Yuki.

12:24.869 --> 12:27.204
You're so sure about it.

12:27.288 --> 12:29.206
Because it's the truth.

12:29.290 --> 12:33.502
That's how solid Yuki's position
as the next president is.

12:34.086 --> 12:35.421
And as usual,

12:35.504 --> 12:37.423
there should be three pairs of candidates

12:37.506 --> 12:39.925
aiming for the position
of president and vice president.

12:40.009 --> 12:40.885
In fact,

12:40.968 --> 12:42.470
among the first-years in junior high,

12:43.137 --> 12:44.972
<i>there were six pairs,
including Yuki and me.</i>

12:45.055 --> 12:47.224
<i>A total of 12 candidates.</i>

12:47.308 --> 12:48.726
<i>That many?</i>

12:48.809 --> 12:50.019
However,

12:50.102 --> 12:51.979
at the general meeting
before the election,

12:52.062 --> 12:53.981
half of them withdrew.

12:54.064 --> 12:56.192
What's a general meeting?

12:56.275 --> 12:58.694
It's like a debate between students.

12:59.195 --> 13:00.321
For example,

13:00.404 --> 13:03.407
if the mediation
between the soccer and baseball clubs

13:03.491 --> 13:05.326
can't reach a consensus no matter what,

13:05.409 --> 13:09.079
we'll hold a general meeting
and settle it.

13:09.663 --> 13:12.833
<i>I knew there were occasional events
in the auditorium.</i>

13:12.917 --> 13:14.418
<i>So that's what it was.</i>

13:15.169 --> 13:16.212
Then,

13:16.295 --> 13:17.671
why did half of them withdraw

13:17.755 --> 13:19.715
because of the general meeting?

13:19.798 --> 13:22.551
If the ones holding the meeting
are election candidates,

13:22.635 --> 13:24.803
it's the same as the primary election.

13:24.887 --> 13:28.224
The candidates will have a battle
of opinions and decide the winner.

13:28.307 --> 13:29.642
Most of the students

13:29.725 --> 13:32.228
will think that's how
their standing is decided.

13:32.811 --> 13:34.021
I see.

13:34.605 --> 13:36.524
That's how they usually fight it out.

13:36.607 --> 13:39.902
In the end, it'll narrow down
to three pairs of candidates

13:40.402 --> 13:42.988
Well, not everyone who wants
to run for presidency

13:43.072 --> 13:45.783
will join the student council.

13:45.866 --> 13:46.700
Even so,

13:46.784 --> 13:48.619
things are clearly different this year.

13:49.203 --> 13:50.996
It means everyone has given up.

13:51.080 --> 13:53.207
They think they can't beat Yuki.

13:54.500 --> 13:55.626
<i>What?</i>

13:55.709 --> 13:57.628
<i>He looks so nonchalant.</i>

13:57.711 --> 13:59.296
<i>What's the meaning of this?</i>

13:59.380 --> 14:03.008
<i>Is he used to coming
to family restaurants with girls?</i>

14:03.759 --> 14:08.013
The merits of being the president
at this school go without saying.

14:08.097 --> 14:09.056
In fact,

14:09.139 --> 14:12.017
the title of student council
president is so valuable.

14:12.101 --> 14:14.436
- <i>I was thinking why the straw didn't work.</i>
- In the election a few years ago,

14:14.520 --> 14:16.021
- <i>When did I...</i>
- there were still people

14:16.105 --> 14:18.774
who played dirty behind the scenes.

14:19.984 --> 14:21.318
But thanks to that,

14:21.402 --> 14:24.822
we can have a clean election now.

14:27.575 --> 14:29.326
Alya, are you listening to me?

14:29.410 --> 14:30.619
Of course I am.

14:30.703 --> 14:32.913
I was just distracted by the parfait.

14:32.997 --> 14:33.956
I see.

14:34.039 --> 14:36.292
Well, it does look delicious.

14:36.375 --> 14:37.543
<i>What the heck?</i>

14:37.626 --> 14:38.919
<i>In the first place,</i>

14:39.003 --> 14:40.546
<i>it's because of your attitude</i>

14:40.629 --> 14:42.506
<i>that I lost my pace.</i>

14:46.093 --> 14:47.344
<i>That's right.</i>

14:47.428 --> 14:48.888
<i>If he doesn't realize that,</i>

14:48.971 --> 14:50.973
<i>I'll make him.</i>

14:51.473 --> 14:52.391
Hey.

14:52.474 --> 14:54.184
Do you want a bite?

14:54.268 --> 14:55.936
No, it's okay.

14:56.020 --> 14:57.897
You said it looked delicious.

14:57.980 --> 15:00.190
No need to be shy.

15:00.733 --> 15:02.526
Here, eat up.

15:03.068 --> 15:06.030
No, I can use a new spoon.

15:06.113 --> 15:08.490
Calling the staff would cause them trouble

15:08.574 --> 15:10.200
and an extra spoon to wash.

15:10.784 --> 15:11.994
But...

15:12.077 --> 15:13.329
Come on, just eat!

15:13.412 --> 15:15.539
This little thing is normal in Russia.

15:15.623 --> 15:16.624
What? Really?

15:17.583 --> 15:19.376
<i>So it's a lie.</i>

15:19.960 --> 15:21.712
Open up!

15:21.795 --> 15:24.089
<i>She finally said it!</i>

15:27.426 --> 15:34.433
<i>A deep indirect kiss!</i>

15:36.393 --> 15:37.603
It's so sweet.

15:37.686 --> 15:38.604
Is it?

15:45.194 --> 15:46.695
<i>Is that</i>

15:46.779 --> 15:47.738
<i>Taniyama?</i>

15:50.115 --> 15:50.991
So,

15:51.075 --> 15:53.494
what can I do to beat Yuki?

15:53.577 --> 15:56.914
Even if you go head-to-head,
you have no chance of winning.

15:56.997 --> 15:59.750
So you have to appeal for votes
in a different way from Yuki.

15:59.833 --> 16:01.502
How should I go about it?

16:01.585 --> 16:04.213
For example, like President Kenzaki now.

16:04.797 --> 16:06.298
<i>In last year's election,</i>

16:06.382 --> 16:08.717
<i>a former junior high president
also competed.</i>

16:09.218 --> 16:10.511
<i>Even so,</i>

16:10.594 --> 16:12.721
<i>President Kenzaki was elected.</i>

16:13.263 --> 16:14.723
<i>During junior high,</i>

16:14.807 --> 16:17.726
<i>President Kenzaki wasn't
a student council member, right?</i>

16:17.810 --> 16:18.811
<i>That's right.</i>

16:18.894 --> 16:20.396
<i>The reason he was elected</i>

16:20.479 --> 16:22.022
<i>was because of a secret plan.</i>

16:22.106 --> 16:22.982
<i>A secret plan?</i>

16:23.649 --> 16:27.361
<i>A member of the newspaper club
saw previously underachieving Kenzaki</i>

16:27.444 --> 16:28.904
<i>running for president</i>

16:28.988 --> 16:31.365
<i>and found it interesting,
so he did an interview.</i>

16:31.448 --> 16:33.325
<i>At first, the newspaper club member</i>

16:33.409 --> 16:35.411
<i>was probably only half-joking.</i>

16:36.161 --> 16:37.454
<i>But as the series went on,</i>

16:37.538 --> 16:39.123
<i>his appearance visibly changed</i>

16:39.206 --> 16:40.749
<i>and his grades improved.</i>

16:40.833 --> 16:43.836
<i>It seemed like a real success story,</i>

16:43.919 --> 16:45.796
<i>so everyone started to cheer for him.</i>

16:46.296 --> 16:47.214
<i>And then,</i>

16:47.297 --> 16:49.758
<i>he got elected successfully.</i>

16:50.342 --> 16:51.427
In short,

16:51.510 --> 16:53.846
I have to create a story
that will garner support?

16:53.929 --> 16:54.847
In other words,

16:54.930 --> 16:58.726
I have to let the students around me
see my hard work and effort?

16:58.809 --> 17:00.769
Your understanding is really impressive.

17:01.895 --> 17:02.771
<i>So,</i>

17:02.855 --> 17:04.773
<i>what are you going to do with that spoon?</i>

17:06.233 --> 17:08.235
<i>What should I do with this spoon?</i>

17:15.576 --> 17:17.119
Well,

17:17.202 --> 17:18.912
can I order something to eat?

17:18.996 --> 17:19.955
What?

17:20.039 --> 17:21.415
Fine by me.

17:23.500 --> 17:25.294
Thank you for waiting.

17:26.003 --> 17:28.005
And this is a new spoon.

17:28.505 --> 17:30.591
Well then, please enjoy your meal.

17:31.884 --> 17:33.510
It was fine.

17:33.594 --> 17:35.387
It's embarrassing for me.

17:35.971 --> 17:37.890
You're panicking over this?

17:37.973 --> 17:40.476
Kuze, you're surprisingly pure.

17:40.559 --> 17:42.978
I thought you'd be used to girls by now.

17:43.479 --> 17:46.857
I'm the one who can't believe
that you can do that

17:46.940 --> 17:48.984
with a straight face.

17:49.068 --> 17:52.488
Do Russians often kiss
indirectly like this?

17:53.363 --> 17:56.116
I wouldn't do this to anyone but you.

17:56.200 --> 17:57.117
Idiot.

17:58.077 --> 17:59.286
<i>Thank you.</i>

17:59.870 --> 18:01.622
Come on, eat up.

18:01.705 --> 18:02.831
It's going to melt.

18:02.915 --> 18:03.916
You're right.

18:05.417 --> 18:07.836
So what should I do specifically

18:07.920 --> 18:10.506
to create a story that garners support
like President Kenzaki?

18:11.507 --> 18:13.217
Let's see.

18:13.300 --> 18:16.512
You have to show them
how hard you work, right?

18:16.595 --> 18:18.680
First, the closing ceremony
of last semester...

18:18.764 --> 18:19.890
Are you referring

18:19.973 --> 18:22.101
to the speeches
of student council members?

18:22.184 --> 18:23.102
That's right.

18:23.185 --> 18:24.311
In fact,

18:24.394 --> 18:28.315
this will be your first time giving
a speech in front of the entire school.

18:28.398 --> 18:31.068
I don't need to tell you
how important it is.

18:31.777 --> 18:34.822
Then what should I say?

18:34.905 --> 18:36.990
Just say whatever you want.

18:37.074 --> 18:39.034
If you express it in your own words,

18:39.118 --> 18:40.702
the audience will understand better.

18:40.786 --> 18:41.829
What?

18:41.912 --> 18:44.039
Don't you have any specific advice?

18:44.623 --> 18:46.208
No need to force yourself.

18:46.291 --> 18:49.336
You can get a lot of support
with what you're doing now.

18:51.213 --> 18:52.297
Really?

18:53.465 --> 18:55.092
What exactly am I doing?

18:55.175 --> 18:57.302
Shower me with more compliments.

18:57.386 --> 18:59.221
<i>That's what I'm talking about.</i>

18:59.304 --> 19:00.514
<i>Darn it.</i>

19:05.477 --> 19:07.980
It's quite spicy for a family restaurant.

19:08.063 --> 19:09.148
Is it good?

19:09.231 --> 19:10.399
Yes, it's all right.

19:10.899 --> 19:11.817
Care for a taste?

19:11.900 --> 19:16.196
<i>No, I don't think she can handle
this level of spiciness.</i>

19:17.364 --> 19:18.532
<i>It looks so spicy.</i>

19:19.032 --> 19:20.742
<i>But if I give up now,</i>

19:20.826 --> 19:24.329
<i>he'll find out
that I don't like spicy food.</i>

19:25.205 --> 19:27.291
Well then, I'll have a bite.

19:33.005 --> 19:35.215
ONE WHOLE CHILI PEPPER

19:38.760 --> 19:40.387
Do it, Aniki.

19:40.470 --> 19:42.014
Alya's tearful eyes

19:42.097 --> 19:44.516
actually excite you, don't they?

19:44.600 --> 19:45.434
No.

19:45.517 --> 19:48.395
You can't do this to Alya.

19:49.271 --> 19:50.606
Get lost!

19:56.111 --> 19:57.529
Forgive me, Alya.

19:58.238 --> 20:00.616
Here, I'll give you
the most delicious part.

20:00.699 --> 20:02.034
Thank you.

20:16.590 --> 20:17.549
Alya?

20:19.092 --> 20:20.636
Idiot.

20:24.640 --> 20:26.183
Are you okay?

20:26.266 --> 20:28.685
What do you mean? I'm fine.

20:28.769 --> 20:30.187
That's good.

20:32.397 --> 20:33.440
By the way,

20:33.523 --> 20:35.442
I wonder what Yuki is planning to do.

20:35.525 --> 20:36.526
What?

20:36.610 --> 20:37.444
I mean,

20:37.527 --> 20:40.405
since you're running with me,

20:40.489 --> 20:42.699
Yuki needs a new part...

20:42.783 --> 20:44.910
vice president candidate, right?

20:45.410 --> 20:46.620
Well,

20:46.703 --> 20:49.206
she's always been popular,

20:49.289 --> 20:52.376
so I think it wouldn't matter
who she partners with.

20:52.459 --> 20:53.543
But normally,

20:53.627 --> 20:55.837
she'd choose
a former student council member.

20:57.422 --> 20:58.799
Come to think of it,

20:58.882 --> 21:00.592
if she brings Taniyama to the election,

21:00.676 --> 21:02.135
it'd be troublesome.

21:02.219 --> 21:03.845
Taniyama? Who's that?

21:03.929 --> 21:05.681
Sayaka Taniyama.

21:05.764 --> 21:06.890
In junior high,

21:06.974 --> 21:10.394
she competed with Yuki
for the presidency until the very end.

21:10.477 --> 21:11.436
You don't know her?

21:11.520 --> 21:12.688
No.

21:13.855 --> 21:15.482
<i>Did she</i>

21:15.565 --> 21:18.235
<i>give up on becoming the president?</i>

21:20.070 --> 21:21.113
Kuze?

21:22.197 --> 21:23.323
Anyway,

21:23.407 --> 21:24.866
I'll find out soon enough

21:25.450 --> 21:26.827
who Yuki's running with.

21:27.953 --> 21:29.871
SEIREN ACADEMY

21:29.955 --> 21:31.373
STUDENT COUNCIL OFFICE

21:32.082 --> 21:34.918
Well then, allow me to introduce everyone.

21:35.460 --> 21:36.378
Ayano.

21:40.882 --> 21:41.883
Kuze?

21:43.969 --> 21:45.887
Nice to meet you.

21:45.971 --> 21:50.392
I'm Ayano Kimishima from Class 1-C.

21:50.892 --> 21:51.727
From now on,

21:51.810 --> 21:53.186
I'll be working with all of you

21:53.270 --> 21:56.398
as the student council's general affairs.

21:56.481 --> 21:58.900
I look forward to working with all of you.

22:00.485 --> 22:01.778
Master Masachika.

22:01.862 --> 22:03.155
As a fellow general affairs,

22:03.238 --> 22:04.906
I look forward to working with you.

22:05.907 --> 22:06.908
Ayano.
